===Etymology 2===
A variant of {{m|en|wroth}}, probably influenced by {{m|en|wrath|pos=noun}} (see [[#Etymology 1|etymology 1]]).<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=1067469857|date=July 2023}}</ref>

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|archaic}} {{synonym of|en|wroth|t=[[full#Adjective|full]] of [[anger#Noun|anger]]; [[wrathful]]}}.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Midsummer Q1|act=II|scene=i|sig=B3|page=14|passage=Take heede the Queene come not vvithin his ſight, <br> For ''{{w|Oberon}}'' is paſſing fell and '''vvrath''': <br> Becauſe that ſhe, as her attendant, hath <br> A louely boy ſtollen, from an Indian king: <br> She neuer had ſo ſvveete a changeling.|footer=Pronounced to rhyme with ''hath''.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1596.2|book=IV|canto=VIII|stanza=43|page=120|passage=VVhereat the Prince full '''vvrath''', his ſtrong right hand <br> In full auengement heaued vp on hie, <br> And ſtroke the Pagan vvith his ſteely brand <br> So ſore, that to his ſaddle bovv thereby <br> He bovved lovv, and ſo a vvhile did lie: {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Douay Bible|OT1|Genesis|40|2–3|pages=122–123|pageref=123|passage=And Pharao being a '''vvrath''' againſt them (for the one vvas chiefe of the cupbearers, the other chiefe baker) he ſent them into the priſon of the captaine of the ſouldiers, in the vvhich [[w:Joseph (Genesis)|Ioſeph]] alſo vvas priſoner.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Poems|poem=Nativity|page=9|passage=Th' old Dragon underground <br> In ſtraiter limits bound, <br> Not half ſo far caſts his uſurped ſvvay, <br> And '''vvrath''' to ſee his Kingdom fail, <br> Svvindges the ſcaly Horrour of his foulded tail.}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Lovel|chapter=A Black Sheep|page=165|passage=Lovel, seldom angry, was violently '''wrath''' with his brother-in-law; and, almost always polite, was at breakfast scarcely civil to Lady Baker.}}
#* {{RQ:Bulwer-Lytton Strange Story|volume=II|chapter=XXXI|page=229|passage=I felt '''wrath''' with her. My heart so cherished my harmless, defenceless Lilian, that I was jealous of the praise taken from her to be bestowed on another.}}

